---
import ProseLayout from '../../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import FaqList from '../../components/FaqList.astro';
import { unloopAppLd } from '../../lib/jsonld';
import { site } from '../../site.config';
---
<ProseLayout
  title="Unloop help and support"
  description="Answers to common questions about Unloop, fixes for when the pause stops appearing, and how to contact support."
  intro="Answers to common questions, fixes for the most common problems, and how to reach a real person."
  jsonLd={[unloopAppLd()]}
>
  <h2 id="contact">Contact support</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email.support}`}>{site.email.support}</a>. {site.responsePromise} It helps to include
    your phone model, Android version, and what you expected to happen.
  </p>

  <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <FaqList />

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>

  <h3 id="accessibility-off">The pause stopped appearing</h3>
  <p>
    Unloop relies on Android’s accessibility service to know when the Reels screen is open. Android can turn this off
    after a system update, if the app is force-stopped, or if the phone’s battery manager closes it. To turn it back on:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open your phone’s <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
    <li>Go to <strong>Accessibility</strong>, then <strong>Installed apps</strong> or <strong>Downloaded apps</strong>.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Unloop</strong> and switch it on.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="muted">Menu names differ between phone brands and Android versions. If you can’t find it, search Settings for “Accessibility”.</p>

  <h3 id="battery">Unloop keeps getting switched off (battery optimization)</h3>
  <p>
    Some phone brands close background apps aggressively to save battery, which can stop Unloop working until you open
    it again. Allowing Unloop to run in the background usually fixes this. The steps vary by brand and software version:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Most Android phones:</strong> Settings → Apps → Unloop → Battery → <em>Unrestricted</em>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Samsung:</strong> Settings → Battery → Background usage limits → <em>Never sleeping apps</em> → add Unloop.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Xiaomi, Redmi and POCO:</strong> Settings → Apps → Manage apps → Unloop → Battery saver → <em>No restrictions</em>,
      and turn on <em>Autostart</em>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>OnePlus, OPPO and realme:</strong> Settings → Battery → App battery management → Unloop → allow background
      activity.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>vivo:</strong> Settings → Battery → Background power consumption management → Unloop → <em>Allow</em>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="muted">
    For step-by-step instructions for your exact phone, <a href="https://dontkillmyapp.com" rel="noopener">dontkillmyapp.com</a>
    keeps an up-to-date guide.
  </p>

  <h3 id="instagram-changed">Instagram updated and the pause misses the Reels screen</h3>
  <p>
    Instagram changes its layout from time to time. Unloop can adapt to many of these changes without an app update, so
    it may start working again without you doing anything. If it doesn’t, please email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email.support}`}>{site.email.support}</a> with your Instagram version (Settings → Apps →
    Instagram).
  </p>

  <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Unloop stores your data on your phone and doesn’t read your messages. Read the <a href="/unloop/privacy/">Unloop privacy policy</a>
    or email <a href={`mailto:${site.email.privacy}`}>{site.email.privacy}</a>.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
